# Why do people follow the crowd?
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy","b":"gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow"}
prompt: "What is an information cascade? When is herding rational?"
next: {"title":"How do we test theories of choice?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/econ-from-zero/102-how-do-we-test-theories-of-choice.cast"}

## Same song, eight worlds
sources:
    - id: salganik2006
      title: Experimental Study of Inequality and Unpredictability in an Artificial Cultural Market
      authors: Salganik, M. J., Dodds, P. S., Watts, D. J.
      year: 2006
      finding: 'Science 311(5762): 854–856. 14,341 participants downloaded 48 previously unknown songs, either independently or seeing earlier downloads in one of eight separate ''worlds''; social influence raised both the inequality and the unpredictability of success.'
      doi: 10.1126/science.1121066
    - id: watts2007
      title: Is Justin Timberlake a Product of Cumulative Advantage?
      authors: Watts, D. J.
      year: 2007
      finding: New York Times Magazine, 15 April 2007. 'Lockdown' by 52metro ranked 26th of 48 in quality (its popularity in the independent condition), yet was No. 1 in one social-influence world and 40th in another.

    icon note size 80 set twemoji x 120 y 585 icon_look picture of "musical note" hidden true
    text song "Lockdown · 52metro" x 340 y 585 font_size 40 hidden true
    text lab "MusicLab 2006\n14,341 listeners · 48 songs" #8f887c cites ["salganik2006"] x 770 y 585 font_size 34 hidden true
    text w0 "cold" #8f887c x 200 y 210 font_size 30 in worlds hidden true
    icon w1 size 44 set twemoji icon_look picture of globe in worlds hidden true
    icon w2 size 44 set twemoji icon_look picture of globe in worlds hidden true
    icon w3 size 44 set twemoji icon_look picture of globe in worlds hidden true
