      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:azkzr0'
    '|a||The easy answer is that people are sheep: they copy, and copying turns luck into hits.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1l8wqad'
    '|b||Maybe. But a download count is information. If you''ve never heard of any of these bands, isn''t what others picked worth knowing?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:19xzd82'
    '|a||Then here''s the puzzle: could every listener be perfectly sensible, and the crowd still end up almost anywhere?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1wdcakg'
    '|b||A download count mixes taste and information. To see the information alone, economists built a game: two urns and a die. The die secretly picks one urn, fifty-fifty, and nobody is told which.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Lisa Anderson and Charles Holt ran it in 1997. One urn holds two light balls and a dark one; the other, two dark and a light one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:837p9x'
    '|b||Six players, one at a time, draw a ball in private, put it back, and say out loud which urn they think it is. Two dollars for a right guess.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:hf4kqn'
    '|a||Player one draws dark, and says dark urn.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:14fu8ep'
    '|b||Player two says dark too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:cpx6x4'
    '|a||I''d trust my own ball. It''s the only thing I actually saw.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1kx6rmr'
    '|b||You''re player three. Your ball is light; players one and two both said dark. Which urn do you name?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:11cz1e0'
    '|b||The dark urn: their words reveal two dark balls, and yours is one light one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Count it. Their words tell you their balls: dark and dark. Yours is light. Two against one: the dark urn is twice as likely.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||So I say dark, and my light ball goes unheard. Nobody behind me can tell what I drew.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:erl7pp'
    '|b||Player four hears three darks, but knows yours tells nothing. Same spot as you: dark, whatever the ball. And so on down the line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1yhg6rc'
    '|a||That''s an information cascade: once the evidence tips by two, everyone after rationally ignores their own. Sushil Bikhchandani, David Hirshleifer and Ivo Welch named it in 1992; Abhijit Banerjee told it with two restaurants.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:fxp9h9'
    '|b||In one real round of their experiment, the first two drew the misleading colour, and all four after them followed, despite holding the right one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:p80dk4'
    '|a||Four of six held the truth in their hands, and the line still said dark. Nobody was foolish. The information just never got out.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:19b894c'
    '|a||So a line of sensible people can lock onto the wrong urn. How often?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Here''s the model''s own arithmetic. Across the bottom, how good each ball is: one half is a coin toss, one is certain.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:xzwi6l'
    '|a||I''d guess almost never. Two unlucky balls in a row can''t be that common.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ns0zm'
    '|b||With balls that match their urn two times in three, how often does a long line lock onto the wrong urn?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1blooja'
    '|b||Watch the curve.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||One line in five. With balls this good, two early ones agree by bad luck more often than you''d think.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||And a longer line doesn''t help. The hundredth player is as stuck as the third: a hundred balls in a hundred hands, and the line only ever hears the first few.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:gh9yol'
    '|b||Each player chooses well for themselves. What nobody counts is what their silence costs the people behind them. Economists call that an informational externality.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:7yy76x'
    '|b||At nine in ten, about one line in a hundred goes wrong. Weak signals, and the line is close to a coin toss.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:iftfn6'
    '|a||For player three: two dark balls against one light one. That''s four chances to two, or two thirds, for the dark urn.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Balls come out in pairs until two in a row agree. A right pair has chance p squared; a wrong pair, one minus p, squared.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:6k80z0'
    '|a||At two thirds, that''s one ninth against four ninths: one wrong line in five.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ieo3ps'
    '|a||So when is following the crowd rational? When others'' choices carry evidence you don''t have, and your own is weak. Every player in the line did the right thing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:r2aezu'
    '|a||Rational, then. But does that make real crowds rational?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||First, cascades are fragile. They rest on a couple of early choices, so one piece of public news can tip the whole line. Bikhchandani and coauthors saw fads that way.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:16hl56x'
    '|a||In Anderson and Holt''s lab, cascades formed in forty-one of the fifty-six rounds where the evidence tipped.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ngjkul'
    '|b||And in a fair share of those moments, people kept their own ball anyway. Across thirteen such experiments, Georg Weizsäcker found people go against their own signal only when the odds against it reach about two to one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:7ggutb'
    '|a||So in the lab, people aren''t too sheepish. If anything, they''re too stubborn.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:15sb9za'
    '|b||Outside the lab, a Beijing restaurant chain showed diners its five most popular dishes. Those dishes sold thirteen to twenty percent more.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:f1oas2'
    '|a||But a crowd can pull for other reasons too: wanting to fit in, or a bandwagon. The music worlds can''t tell those apart from information.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:kkq6n1'
    '|a||How sure are we? That cascades happen in the lab: mostly agreed. How much of real herding, from hit songs to market bubbles, is information rather than conformity: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:vpeg3a'
    '|a||So why do people follow the crowd? Often because it''s smart: other people''s choices are evidence. The catch is that a crowd stops passing its evidence on.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:7s0jtx'
    '|a||Three new cases. A new restaurant fills its tables with friends on opening night. What is it counting on?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:byhi5r'
    '|a||Passers-by read a full room as evidence: to a stranger, a crowd is a signal.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Which of these can break a cascade, and which keep it going? Sort each card.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Five fund managers sell a stock, one after another. The sixth learns that managers two to five each saw the first one sell before deciding. How many independent signals does the line of sellers carry?':
